| `dectxzero` / `net_three/F16` | **Overturn the portability-only grouping. These refer to the same realloc defect.** First-segment allocation already requests at least one byte. A zero-length first segment without LS followed by a zero continuation reaches `realloc(nonNULL,0)` at `dev_dec21143.c:788-789`; the recorded NULL result feeds `CHECK_ALLOCATION` → `exit(1)`. The libc measurement supports this local path, although the NIC witness remains unrun. |
| `loaders_four/F7` | **Uphold failed-seek behavior; retain the loader defect.** `file_ecoff.c:278,332,428,439` ignores seek failure. Reading therefore continues from the previous position and can consume wrong bytes or reach a short-read exit. The exact malformed-file result needs a loader run. |

The artifact prints `ftell=5` after failed **fseek**, but no position after **fseeko**. It also does not itself observe that `realloc(p,0)` freed the old block. Those assertions exceed what this experiment directly measured.

